if 2016's doom was a modern 101 course  in ripping and tearing doom eternal is  your master class in the art of demon  dismemberment its software channels all  the aggression and speed of its  contemporary take on demon blasting into  a brainy or more cerebral dance of death  it challenges you not only to be light  on your feet and quick with your aim but  to be constantly aware of your  environment your adversaries your  capabilities and your limitations  there's a lot to keep track of which can  lead you to struggle getting through the  game's learning curve but during its  strongest moments of which there are  many doom eternal makes you feel like a  monster shredding badass not just  because you're the strongest doom Slayer  but because you're also the smartest the  fundamental changes of doom eternal  compared to doom 2016 are an how you get  the things you need to stay alive back  our dooms glory kilts where you stagger  an enemy to initiate a brutal takedown  which usually includes ripping off a  part of their body and forcibly  integrating it into another part in doom  2016 glory kills turn enemies into  pinatas of health armor and ammo but  eternal changes that equation glory  kills now only give you health while  killing enemies you set on fire with a  new flamethrower gives you armor and  chainsawing enemies gives you ammo you  have to balance all three kill types to  keep yourself going the overall effect  is that you can't just run around  blasting madly you have to run around  blasting rationally every fight in Doom  eternal requires constant calculus do  you have enough bullets in the right gun  to take down this enemy can you damage  someone enough for a quick health boost  while you're on the run should you put  your effort into knocking out the big  guy who's chasing you or take a second  to snipe off the weapons of a distant  monster by making use of doom eternals  new enemy weak points  most fights take place in big elaborate  multi-level arenas adorned with jump  pads and monkey bars that help you get  around quickly  you're also equipped with a double jump  and a quick horizontal dash that lets  you avoid attacks and cross distances  like everything else positioning has to  be on your mind constantly in doom  eternal if you aren't moving you're  dying  if that sounds overwhelming you're right  it definitely can be watching your ammo  counters or your health counters  assessing threats on the battlefield  picking your paths as you move around  arenas knowing when to fire grenades or  to freeze enemies finding guys to set on  fire and hack up with your chainsaw it's  all a lot to keep track of it's easy to  get thrown out of the joy at battle at  points when you're continually calling  up your weapon wheel to see what you've  still got bullets in or trying to swap  to the correct weapon mod to deal with  the monster currently ripping your face  off there are a lot of things you have  to manage in doom eternal and getting  into the rhythm of that management can  take a while  an eternal can definitely be frustrating  especially in summer eanes where it's  easy to accidentally get stuck in a  corner or back straight over a cliff  eternal isn't a mindless shooter where  you can get into a flow and let your  muscle-memory and reflexes do the work  it's a mind full shooter where every  second requires you to be plotting your  next move especially as you're getting  used to it constantly switching between  attacks and chasing enemies for pickups  can feel antithetical to the fast and  explosive approach players expect from  doom but while it all can be a bit much  eternal is brimming with moments when  all the pieces come together especially  after a few hours of getting the hang of  them it's like the twitch shooter  equivalent of a really great puzzle game  where your success comes from a full  understanding of every single systems  intricacies and your mind and body unify  to execute some ridiculous gory mayhem  doom eternals greatly increased mobility  and creative level design or where the  game really kicks into a metal guitar  solo and start shredding  especially in its best designed arenas  you're always repositioning taking  opportunities to fill your Larter's with  health and ammo and prioritizing threats  to tune the fight to your liking once  you get the rhythm of eternal it becomes  a brilliant extension of what made doom  2016 so cool and eternal is great at  providing heart-pounding moments when  you barely manage to slice off an  opponent's head just in time to shower  yourself with health and cheap death  then spin around and blast a big foe  with a rocket suddenly tipping the odds  in your favor just about every fight  feels like a speeding train seconds from  going off the rails with disaster only  averted because you're so damn good at  killing stuff there are a ton of fights  in Doom eternal and nearly every one of  them is a heart-pounding  white-knuckle struggle for survival well  the intricacies of combat are the big  focus in doom eternal there's a lot of  other stuff going on too there's an even  bigger focus on platforming and puzzling  out how to traverse levels and find the  myriad secrets and upgrades scattered  within them isn't welcome breather  between fights the platforming is still  a bit iffy at times especially when you  need to make a long jump to grab monkey  bars or sticky walls but falls into the  abyss no longer kill you  making these portions of the game pretty  forgiving there's also a fairly involved  story stretch through doom eternal  although good luck following it if you  don't take the time to read the many  collectible or drops scattered around a  turtle's approach to its storytelling  feels like a fundamental shift from the  satirical jokey approach in 2016 s doom  that game was about an energy company  that got rich off devil worship and a  protagonist who would literally punched  the radio's trying to give him context  for his constant mutilations eternal is  entirely more self-serious about Hell  invading earth filled with unexplained  proper nouns events and characters it  acts like you should be intimately  familiar with  and now you see to defy the call maker  herself and as your people's time now to  give penance just as it was mine knowing  what's going on isn't a necessary  component to enjoying the game which is  good because the story is completely  confusing doom eternal also features  master levels which are remixed story  missions meant to offer new and greater  challenges and a multiplayer mode but  neither were available ahead of launch I  will be sinking some time and to doom  eternals additional offerings after  launch and will provide a full review  and a final score after I've had a  chance to test them out with its  intricate combat in level designs doom  eternal manages to elevate all the  things that may do 2016 work so well its  combat is quick and chaotic but it  requires you to constantly analyze  everything that's happening in order to  come out victorious eternal takes some  time to get used to but find its rhythm  and it will reward you with a stream of  ridiculous intense moments that will  scratch your demon slaying itch all  while making you feel like a combat  survive  [Applause]
 

